Can DeFi lending turn crypto holdings into everyday spending power?

Vlad Kamyshov, CEO of EVAA, and Alex Onufriychuk, CMO of EVAA, join Kolo Podcast #5 to explore how lending, crypto cards, and payments could bring DeFi into everyday life.

Hosted by Pavlo Luchkovskyi, CEO of kolo.xyz.

In this episode, we discuss borrowing crypto to fund purchases, the risks behind DeFi lending, how liquidations work, and what a connection between Kolo and EVAA could mean for crypto payments. We also hear the story behind a cold wallet on Everest and explore the balance between marketing hype and responsibility.

If you’re building on TON, exploring crypto payments, or simply want to understand the possibilities and risks of DeFi lending, this episode is for you.

#Crypto #DeFi #TON #CryptoLending #EVAA #KoloPodcast

⸻

💡 What You’ll Learn

• Vlad and Alex’s journeys into crypto and why hackathons matter
• The cold-wallet-on-Everest story and lessons in handling publicity
• How crypto teams balance marketing hype with responsibility
• How DeFi loans could help fund everyday purchases
• The risks of crypto lending and how on-chain liquidations work
• How lending, crypto cards, and payments could work together
• TON’s potential to bring crypto payments to more people
• How large holders influence lending markets and what DeFi could look like in five years

⸻

👥 Meet Vlad Kamyshov & Alex Onufriychuk

